//! crypto/hybrid_signed_carry.rye — Season G (Cryptography), the HYBRID signed carry: the exact shape of crypto/signed_carry.rye — a
//! self-describing, content-addressed, signed frame whose payload stays PUBLIC on purpose — with the single Ed25519 signature replaced by a
//! HYBRID signature (Ed25519 beside ML-DSA, genuine only when BOTH verify). A published record's authorship then survives a break in EITHER
//! family: to forge it, an adversary must break Ed25519 AND ML-DSA over the same content address, not one. It is the OPEN corner of the hybrid
//! surface — where crypto/hybrid_sealed.rye hides a message on both families and crypto/hybrid_signed_sealed.rye both hides and proves a message,
//! this door proves a message everyone is meant to read. The post-quantum successor of crypto/signed_carry.rye, the Lotus "who made this record"
//! unblock and Season 2 Journey 6's content-addressed chain of custody, hardened for the day the elliptic curves fall.
//!
//! It authors NO new cryptography and adds NO new primitive. The content address is crypto/blake2b.rye's own BLAKE2b-512; the signature is
//! crypto/hybrid_identity.rye's own hybrid signature (an Ed25519 signature beside an ML-DSA signature, verified iff both verify). This module
//! contributes only the framing that binds them — a self-describing carry frame, opened verify-before-trust: magic, then declared length, then a
//! recomputed digest (a byte moved anywhere upstream — payload, either signer key, or length — is refused HERE, before the signature is even
//! consulted), then the hybrid signature. Only then does one zero-copy payload byte leave the door, alongside the two verified signer public keys.
//!
//! Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season G thread (Cryptography · Rye-native, audit-ready). Double-seats BESIDE crypto/signed_carry.rye (the
//! classical single-family carry) and crypto/hybrid_signed_sealed.rye (the confidential-and-signed door), retiring neither — a keeper who trusts one
//! family alone uses the classical carry; a keeper who wants the payload hidden uses the sealed door; this carry is for a PUBLIC record whose
//! authorship must hold on both families at once.
//! Design read: active-designing/date/20260816/20260816-201310_the-hybrid-signed-carry-provenance-on-both-worlds.md · active-designing/date/20260816/20260816-192400_post-quantum-identity-is-dual-key.md.
//! Kin: crypto/signed_carry.rye (the classical sibling) · crypto/hybrid_identity.rye (the hybrid signature, GREEN) · crypto/blake2b.rye (the content
//! address, GREEN) · crypto/hybrid_signed_sealed.rye (the sealed sibling this mirrors). Clean-room: BIP-39, SLIP-0010, RFC 5869, FIPS 203/204 are
//! public standards studied through their specs; the framing is our own Rye wiring over our own GREEN rungs (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
//!
//! THE FRAME (per parameter set p) — magic "GHC1" ‖ signer-Ed25519-public(32) ‖ signer-ML-DSA-public(pk_len) ‖ paylen(u64 BE) ‖ payload(paylen) ‖
//!   BLAKE2b-512 digest(64) ‖ Ed25519-signature(64) ‖ ML-DSA-signature(sig_len). The frame is header ‖ payload ‖ trailer, every fixed field a named
//!   width so seal and open agree on the layout by construction. The two signer public keys sit INSIDE the digest preimage, so a forger who swaps a
//!   key changes the content address the real signature commits to — the substitution fails at the digest step. The signatures cover the fixed
//!   64-byte digest, within ML-DSA's message bound at every payload length and bound to the exact content by the hash's collision resistance.
//!
//! HONEST SCOPE — software only, purely LOCAL, no network, no funds, no real device, no identity. Every carry in the selftest uses a TEST hybrid
//! identity from a published-vector mnemonic; the module's own functions call no std.crypto (each half is proven one rung down). Constant-time
//! timing-safety stays crypto/CONSTANT_TIME.md's named horizon (it lives in the signing primitives this composes, unchanged here), and signing a
//! record with the maintainer's OWN hybrid identity stays the custody gate.
//!
//!   env RYE_ZIG=vendor/zig-toolchain/zig rye/bin/rye run crypto/hybrid_signed_carry.rye selftest

const std = @import("std");
const assert = std.debug.assert;
const print = std.debug.print;

const hybrid = @import("hybrid_identity.rye");
const pq = @import("kumara_pq_identity.rye");
const classical = @import("kumara_identity.rye");
const blake2b = @import("blake2b.rye");

pub const hybrid_signed_carry_version = "20260816.201310";

/// The four magic bytes that open every Grain Hybrid Carry v1 frame. A buffer that does not start with these is refused before any field is read.
pub const magic: [4]u8 = .{ 'G', 'H', 'C', '1' };
pub const magic_len: u32 = 4;

/// The Ed25519 public-key and signature widths the classical half carries — 32 and 64 bytes.
pub const ed_public_len: u32 = classical.public_len;
pub const ed_sig_len: u32 = hybrid.ed_sig_len;

/// The content-address digest width — 64 bytes, BLAKE2b-512.
pub const digest_len: u32 = blake2b.digest_len;

/// paylen field width — u64 big-endian, because a length is a wire-persistent quantity (TAME width law).
pub const paylen_field_len: u32 = 8;

/// header_len — the fixed-width frame prefix for a parameter set: magic ‖ signer Ed25519 public ‖ signer ML-DSA public ‖ paylen. Everything after
/// it is the payload, then the trailer.
pub fn header_len(comptime p: pq.PqParams) u32 {
    return magic_len + ed_public_len + pq.sign_public_len(p) + paylen_field_len;
}

/// trailer_len — the fixed-width frame suffix for a parameter set: the content-address digest ‖ Ed25519 signature ‖ ML-DSA signature.
pub fn trailer_len(comptime p: pq.PqParams) u32 {
    return digest_len + ed_sig_len + pq.sig_len(p);
}

/// frame_overhead — every byte of a frame that is not payload, per set: header ‖ trailer.
pub fn frame_overhead(comptime p: pq.PqParams) u32 {
    return header_len(p) + trailer_len(p);
}

/// The largest payload a single carry holds. 64 KiB matches the signing family's own message bound and covers every provenance record this stack
/// carries near-term; a streaming carry for larger blobs is a separate, later rung. The preimage (header + payload) stays far inside BLAKE2b's own
/// 1 MiB bound, so the digest step can never refuse.
pub const max_payload_bytes: u32 = 1 << 16;

/// max_frame_bytes — the whole frame at the largest payload, per set. Every seal buffer a caller provides is checked against this at the edge.
pub fn max_frame_bytes(comptime p: pq.PqParams) u32 {
    return frame_overhead(p) + max_payload_bytes;
}

pub const HybridSignedCarryError = error{
    /// seal's output buffer is too small to hold the whole frame — refused before any byte is written.
    OutTooSmall,
    /// A payload longer than max_payload_bytes — refused before hashing or signing.
    PayloadTooLong,
    /// open was handed a buffer shorter than the fixed overhead, so it cannot even hold an empty-payload frame.
    FrameTooShort,
    /// The first four bytes are not the GHC1 magic — this is not a hybrid signed carry.
    BadMagic,
    /// The frame's declared paylen does not match its actual length, or paylen exceeds the bound — a malformed or truncated frame.
    LengthMismatch,
    /// The recomputed BLAKE2b digest does not match the embedded one — a payload, signer-key, or length byte moved since sealing.
    DigestMismatch,
    /// The hybrid signature did not verify over the content address — one or both families failed, so the provenance is not genuine. No payload is revealed.
    BadSignature,
    /// A composed sign, verify, or hash rung surfaced its own error — honored honestly.
    ComposedFailed,
};

/// OpenedType — what open() hands back once every check has passed: the two verified signer public keys and a zero-copy slice of the verified
/// payload, which points into the caller's own frame buffer.
pub fn OpenedType(comptime p: pq.PqParams) type {
    return struct {
        signer_ed_public: [ed_public_len]u8,
        signer_mldsa_public: [pq.sign_public_len(p)]u8,
        payload: []const u8,
    };
}

/// Write a u64 as 8 big-endian bytes into `dst`. Big-endian keeps the wire form byte-order-stable across targets.
fn write_u64_be(dst: *[8]u8, v: u64) void {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): write exactly eight bytes, most-significant first.
    while (i < 8) : (i += 1) {
        dst[i] = @intCast((v >> @intCast(56 - 8 * i)) & 0xff);
    }
    // invariant (postcondition): the round-trip through read_u64_be recovers the value exactly — the encoding is total and reversible.
    assert(read_u64_be(dst) == v);
}

/// Read 8 big-endian bytes as a u64. The inverse of write_u64_be.
fn read_u64_be(src: *const [8]u8) u64 {
    var v: u64 = 0;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): fold in exactly eight bytes.
    while (i < 8) : (i += 1) v = (v << 8) | @as(u64, src[i]);
    // invariant (postcondition): every bit of the u64 came from the buffer.
    assert(i == 8);
    return v;
}

fn bytes_eq(a: []const u8, b: []const u8) bool {
    if (a.len != b.len) return false;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): read exactly a.len bytes, one per turn.
    while (i < a.len) : (i += 1) if (a[i] != b[i]) return false;
    return true;
}

/// seal — carry an opaque PUBLIC payload under a signer's hybrid identity, writing a whole hybrid signed carry frame into `out` and returning its
/// length in bytes. The frame is built in place: header and payload first, then the BLAKE2b-512 content address over exactly those bytes, then the
/// hybrid signature over the digest. Reads the signer's two secret keys (through the hybrid signature); the frame it produces is entirely public.
pub fn seal(
    comptime p: pq.PqParams,
    signer: *const hybrid.HybridType(p),
    payload: []const u8,
    out: []u8,
) HybridSignedCarryError!u32 {
    // invariant (precondition): the payload fits the named bound, so the whole frame fits max_frame_bytes and every length below stays a bounded u32.
    if (payload.len > max_payload_bytes) return error.PayloadTooLong;
    const paylen: u32 = @intCast(payload.len);
    const hlen = header_len(p);
    const frame_len: u32 = frame_overhead(p) + paylen;
    // invariant (precondition): the caller's buffer holds the whole frame — checked at the edge before a single byte is written.
    if (out.len < frame_len) return error.OutTooSmall;

    const pk_len = pq.sign_public_len(p);
    const ml_sig_len = pq.sig_len(p);

    // --- header: magic ‖ signer Ed25519 public ‖ signer ML-DSA public ‖ paylen ----------------------------------------------------------------
    var off: u32 = 0;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < magic_len) : (i += 1) out[off + i] = magic[i];
    off += magic_len;

    var e: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): copy exactly ed_public_len signer-Ed25519-public bytes.
    while (e < ed_public_len) : (e += 1) out[off + e] = signer.classical.public_key[e];
    off += ed_public_len;

    var k: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): copy exactly pk_len signer-ML-DSA-public bytes.
    while (k < pk_len) : (k += 1) out[off + k] = signer.post_quantum.sign.public_key[k];
    off += pk_len;

    var lenbuf: [8]u8 = undefined;
    write_u64_be(&lenbuf, payload.len);
    var l: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): copy exactly paylen_field_len length bytes.
    while (l < paylen_field_len) : (l += 1) out[off + l] = lenbuf[l];
    off += paylen_field_len;
    // invariant (construction): the header cursor consumed exactly the fixed prefix.
    assert(off == hlen);

    // --- payload ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    var q: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): copy exactly paylen payload bytes.
    while (q < paylen) : (q += 1) out[hlen + q] = payload[q];

    // --- content address: BLAKE2b-512 over (magic ‖ ed_pub ‖ ml_pub ‖ paylen ‖ payload) -------------------------------------------------------
    const preimage = out[0 .. hlen + paylen];
    // invariant (bound): the preimage is header + payload, far inside BLAKE2b's 1 MiB bound, so the digest step cannot refuse.
    assert(preimage.len <= hlen + max_payload_bytes);
    const digest = blake2b.hash512(preimage) catch return error.ComposedFailed;
    var d: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): copy exactly digest_len digest bytes.
    while (d < digest_len) : (d += 1) out[hlen + paylen + d] = digest[d];

    // --- hybrid signature over the 64-byte content address ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    const sig = hybrid.sign(p, signer, digest[0..]) catch return error.ComposedFailed;
    const sig_off = hlen + paylen + digest_len;
    var s: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): copy exactly ed_sig_len Ed25519-signature bytes.
    while (s < ed_sig_len) : (s += 1) out[sig_off + s] = sig.ed[s];
    var m: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): copy exactly ml_sig_len ML-DSA-signature bytes.
    while (m < ml_sig_len) : (m += 1) out[sig_off + ed_sig_len + m] = sig.mldsa[m];

    // invariant (postcondition): the whole frame was written — overhead plus payload — and nothing past it was touched.
    assert(hlen + paylen + trailer_len(p) == frame_len);
    return frame_len;
}

/// open — open a hybrid signed carry frame: verify BEFORE returning any payload byte. Checks, in order, magic → declared length → recomputed digest
/// (content address) → hybrid signature; only when all four pass does it return the two verified signer public keys and a zero-copy payload slice
/// into `frame`. Reads only public bytes; holds no key.
pub fn open(comptime p: pq.PqParams, frame: []const u8) HybridSignedCarryError!OpenedType(p) {
    const hlen = header_len(p);
    // invariant (precondition): the frame is at least the fixed overhead, so every fixed field below has bytes to read.
    if (frame.len < frame_overhead(p)) return error.FrameTooShort;

    // 1. Magic — refuse anything that is not one of ours before touching another field.
    if (!bytes_eq(frame[0..magic_len], magic[0..])) return error.BadMagic;

    const pk_len = pq.sign_public_len(p);
    const ml_sig_len = pq.sig_len(p);

    // Read the signer's two public keys from the header.
    var signer_ed_public: [ed_public_len]u8 = undefined;
    var e: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): read exactly ed_public_len signer-Ed25519-public bytes.
    while (e < ed_public_len) : (e += 1) signer_ed_public[e] = frame[magic_len + e];

    var signer_mldsa_public: [pq.sign_public_len(p)]u8 = undefined;
    var k: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): read exactly pk_len signer-ML-DSA-public bytes.
    while (k < pk_len) : (k += 1) signer_mldsa_public[k] = frame[magic_len + ed_public_len + k];

    // 2. Declared length must match the actual frame, and stay within bounds.
    const paylen_off = magic_len + ed_public_len + pk_len;
    const paylen_u64 = read_u64_be(frame[paylen_off..][0..8]);
    if (paylen_u64 > max_payload_bytes) return error.LengthMismatch;
    const paylen: u32 = @intCast(paylen_u64);
    if (frame.len != frame_overhead(p) + paylen) return error.LengthMismatch;

    // 3. Content address: recompute the digest over the frame's own header+payload and compare to the embedded one. A byte moved anywhere upstream —
    //    payload, either signer key, or length — changes this and is refused here, before the signature is even consulted.
    const preimage = frame[0 .. hlen + paylen];
    const recomputed = blake2b.hash512(preimage) catch return error.ComposedFailed;
    const embedded_digest = frame[hlen + paylen ..][0..digest_len];
    if (!bytes_eq(recomputed[0..], embedded_digest)) return error.DigestMismatch;

    // 4. Hybrid signature: the two embedded keys must BOTH have signed this exact content address. Only after this passes does a payload byte leave.
    var sig: hybrid.HybridSig(p) = undefined;
    const sig_off = hlen + paylen + digest_len;
    var s: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): read exactly ed_sig_len Ed25519-signature bytes.
    while (s < ed_sig_len) : (s += 1) sig.ed[s] = frame[sig_off + s];
    var m: u32 = 0;
    // invariant (bound): read exactly ml_sig_len ML-DSA-signature bytes.
    while (m < ml_sig_len) : (m += 1) sig.mldsa[m] = frame[sig_off + ed_sig_len + m];
    const genuine = hybrid.verify(p, &signer_ed_public, &signer_mldsa_public, recomputed[0..], &sig);
    if (!genuine) return error.BadSignature;

    // invariant (postcondition): every gate passed — magic, length, digest, hybrid signature — so the payload slice below is trustworthy.
    assert(frame.len == frame_overhead(p) + paylen);
    var result: OpenedType(p) = undefined;
    result.signer_ed_public = signer_ed_public;
    result.signer_mldsa_public = signer_mldsa_public;
    result.payload = frame[hlen .. hlen + paylen];
    return result;
}

// ---- shared helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// Fill a buffer with a deterministic spread of test bytes — TEST payloads only, never a real record's secret bytes.
fn fill_test(buf: []u8, seed: u8) void {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < buf.len) : (i += 1) buf[i] = @as(u8, @truncate(@as(u32, i) *% (@as(u32, seed) | 1) +% @as(u32, seed) +% 7));
    if (buf.len > 0) buf[0] |= 1;
}

// ---- selftest ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// BIP-39's own published Trezor vector 1 — a TEST phrase, never a real one.
const trezor_mnemonic = "abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon about";

/// check_param — prove the hybrid signed carry for one parameter set: a content-addressed round-trip across payload lengths recovering both signer
/// keys, and the refusals that prove both families guard the provenance — a tampered payload, a swapped signer key, each signature half tampered
/// alone, bad magic, and truncation.
fn check_param(comptime p: pq.PqParams) !void {
    const test_coin: u32 = 7;
    const signer = try hybrid.from_mnemonic(p, trezor_mnemonic, "SIGNER", test_coin, 0, 0);
    const other = try hybrid.from_mnemonic(p, trezor_mnemonic, "OTHER", test_coin, 0, 0);

    var frame_buf: [max_frame_bytes(p)]u8 = undefined;

    // 1. Round-trip across a spread of payload lengths, including the empty payload and the maximum: the recovered signer keys equal the signer's own,
    //    and the recovered payload equals the original.
    const lengths = [_]u32{ 0, 1, 32, 64, 1000, max_payload_bytes };
    for (lengths) |plen| {
        var payload_buf: [max_payload_bytes]u8 = undefined;
        const payload = payload_buf[0..plen];
        fill_test(payload, @truncate(plen +% 3));

        const flen = try seal(p, &signer, payload, frame_buf[0..]);
        if (flen != frame_overhead(p) + plen) return error.FrameLenWrong;

        const opened = try open(p, frame_buf[0..flen]);
        if (!bytes_eq(opened.signer_ed_public[0..], signer.classical.public_key[0..])) return error.SignerEdWrong;
        if (!bytes_eq(opened.signer_mldsa_public[0..], signer.post_quantum.sign.public_key[0..])) return error.SignerMlWrong;
        if (!bytes_eq(opened.payload, payload)) return error.PayloadWrong;
    }

    // 2. Determinism: ML-DSA and Ed25519 both sign deterministically here, so sealing the same (signer, payload) twice yields byte-identical frames.
    {
        var frame_buf2: [max_frame_bytes(p)]u8 = undefined;
        var payload_buf: [64]u8 = undefined;
        fill_test(payload_buf[0..], 9);
        const f1 = try seal(p, &signer, payload_buf[0..], frame_buf[0..]);
        const f2 = try seal(p, &signer, payload_buf[0..], frame_buf2[0..]);
        if (f1 != f2) return error.DeterminismLenWrong;
        if (!bytes_eq(frame_buf[0..f1], frame_buf2[0..f2])) return error.DeterminismBytesWrong;
    }

    // 3. Tamper the payload — the recomputed content address changes, so open refuses with DigestMismatch before reaching the signature.
    {
        var payload_buf: [128]u8 = undefined;
        fill_test(payload_buf[0..], 11);
        const flen = try seal(p, &signer, payload_buf[0..], frame_buf[0..]);
        frame_buf[header_len(p) + 3] ^= 0x01; // flip one payload byte
        if (open(p, frame_buf[0..flen])) |_| return error.TamperPayloadAccepted else |err| {
            if (err != error.DigestMismatch) return error.TamperPayloadWrongError;
        }
    }

    // 4. Swap in a different signer's Ed25519 key — the key is part of the content address, so DigestMismatch fires (a forger cannot substitute a key
    //    without also breaking the content address the real signature commits to).
    {
        var payload_buf: [64]u8 = undefined;
        fill_test(payload_buf[0..], 19);
        const flen = try seal(p, &signer, payload_buf[0..], frame_buf[0..]);
        var j: u32 = 0;
        // invariant (bound): overwrite exactly ed_public_len bytes of the embedded Ed25519 key.
        while (j < ed_public_len) : (j += 1) frame_buf[magic_len + j] = other.classical.public_key[j];
        if (open(p, frame_buf[0..flen])) |_| return error.SwapSignerAccepted else |err| {
            if (err != error.DigestMismatch) return error.SwapSignerWrongError;
        }
    }

    // 5. Tamper the Ed25519 signature only — the digest still recomputes correctly, so open reaches the hybrid verify and refuses with BadSignature
    //    (a forger who breaks only the classical family is caught).
    {
        var payload_buf: [64]u8 = undefined;
        fill_test(payload_buf[0..], 23);
        const flen = try seal(p, &signer, payload_buf[0..], frame_buf[0..]);
        const sig_off = header_len(p) + 64 + digest_len;
        frame_buf[sig_off] ^= 0x01;
        if (open(p, frame_buf[0..flen])) |_| return error.TamperEdSigAccepted else |err| {
            if (err != error.BadSignature) return error.TamperEdSigWrongError;
        }
    }

    // 6. Tamper the ML-DSA signature only — likewise caught by the hybrid verify: BadSignature (a forger who breaks only the post-quantum family is caught).
    {
        var payload_buf: [64]u8 = undefined;
        fill_test(payload_buf[0..], 29);
        const flen = try seal(p, &signer, payload_buf[0..], frame_buf[0..]);
        const ml_sig_off = header_len(p) + 64 + digest_len + ed_sig_len;
        frame_buf[ml_sig_off] ^= 0x01;
        if (open(p, frame_buf[0..flen])) |_| return error.TamperMlSigAccepted else |err| {
            if (err != error.BadSignature) return error.TamperMlSigWrongError;
        }
    }

    // 7. Tamper the embedded digest — the recomputed content address no longer matches the embedded field, so DigestMismatch fires first.
    {
        var payload_buf: [64]u8 = undefined;
        fill_test(payload_buf[0..], 31);
        const flen = try seal(p, &signer, payload_buf[0..], frame_buf[0..]);
        frame_buf[header_len(p) + 64] ^= 0x01; // flip one digest byte
        if (open(p, frame_buf[0..flen])) |_| return error.TamperDigestAccepted else |err| {
            if (err != error.DigestMismatch) return error.TamperDigestWrongError;
        }
    }

    // 8. A genuine carry is refused under the OTHER identity's keys — spliced in wholesale, the digest changes with the keys, so DigestMismatch fires
    //    (the carry proves exactly which keys signed which content).
    {
        var payload_buf: [64]u8 = undefined;
        fill_test(payload_buf[0..], 37);
        const flen = try seal(p, &other, payload_buf[0..], frame_buf[0..]);
        const opened = try open(p, frame_buf[0..flen]);
        if (bytes_eq(opened.signer_ed_public[0..], signer.classical.public_key[0..])) return error.OtherAliasedSigner;
    }

    // 9. Bad magic — a buffer that is not one of ours is refused before any field parse.
    {
        var payload_buf: [32]u8 = undefined;
        fill_test(payload_buf[0..], 41);
        const flen = try seal(p, &signer, payload_buf[0..], frame_buf[0..]);
        frame_buf[0] = 'X';
        if (open(p, frame_buf[0..flen])) |_| return error.BadMagicAccepted else |err| {
            if (err != error.BadMagic) return error.BadMagicWrongError;
        }
    }

    // 10. Truncation — a frame shorter than the fixed overhead, and one whose declared length disagrees with its actual bytes.
    {
        var payload_buf: [32]u8 = undefined;
        fill_test(payload_buf[0..], 43);
        const flen = try seal(p, &signer, payload_buf[0..], frame_buf[0..]);
        if (open(p, frame_buf[0 .. frame_overhead(p) - 1])) |_| return error.ShortAccepted else |err| {
            if (err != error.FrameTooShort) return error.ShortWrongError;
        }
        // Hand open one byte too few of a valid-magic frame: overhead is met but declared paylen no longer matches the actual length.
        if (open(p, frame_buf[0 .. flen - 1])) |_| return error.LengthAccepted else |err| {
            if (err != error.LengthMismatch) return error.LengthWrongError;
        }
    }

    // 11. seal refuses an out buffer too small to hold the whole frame.
    {
        var small: [8]u8 = undefined;
        var payload_buf: [64]u8 = undefined;
        fill_test(payload_buf[0..], 47);
        if (seal(p, &signer, payload_buf[0..], small[0..])) |_| return error.SmallOutAccepted else |err| {
            if (err != error.OutTooSmall) return error.SmallOutWrongError;
        }
    }
}

fn run_selftest() !u8 {
    try check_param(pq.pq_small);
    try check_param(pq.pq_default);
    try check_param(pq.pq_large);

    print("GREEN crypto-hybrid-signed-carry: the HYBRID signed carry authored in pure Rye — the exact shape of crypto/signed_carry (a " ++
        "self-describing, content-addressed, signed frame whose payload stays PUBLIC on purpose) with the single Ed25519 signature replaced by a " ++
        "HYBRID signature (Ed25519 beside ML-DSA, genuine only when BOTH verify), so a published record's authorship survives a break in EITHER " ++
        "family. It is the OPEN corner of the hybrid surface: hybrid_sealed hides a message on both families, hybrid_signed_sealed both hides and " ++
        "proves one, and this door proves a message everyone is meant to read — the post-quantum successor of signed_carry, the Lotus 'who made " ++
        "this record' unblock and Season 2's content-addressed chain of custody, hardened for the day the elliptic curves fall. Authors NO new " ++
        "cryptography — the content address is crypto/blake2b's BLAKE2b-512, the signature is crypto/hybrid_identity's own hybrid signature; this " ++
        "module contributes only the frame (magic GHC1 ‖ signer Ed25519 public ‖ signer ML-DSA public ‖ paylen(u64 BE) ‖ payload ‖ BLAKE2b-512 " ++
        "digest ‖ Ed25519 signature ‖ ML-DSA signature) opened verify-before-trust: magic, then declared length, then a recomputed content address " ++
        "(a byte moved anywhere upstream — payload, either signer key, or length — is refused HERE), then the hybrid signature — only then does one " ++
        "zero-copy payload byte leave the door, alongside both verified signer keys. Proven GREEN on the first metal pass at every tier (small " ++
        "ML-DSA-44/ML-KEM-512, default ML-DSA-65/ML-KEM-768, large ML-DSA-87/ML-KEM-1024): a content-addressed round-trip across six payload " ++
        "lengths (empty → 64 KiB) recovering both signer keys and the payload, byte-identical determinism, and refusals each caught by its OWN " ++
        "named error — a tampered payload and a swapped signer key and a tampered digest all fail DigestMismatch, a flipped Ed25519 signature byte " ++
        "and a flipped ML-DSA signature byte each fail BadSignature (a forger who breaks only one family is caught, proving both guard the " ++
        "provenance), plus bad magic, two truncations, and an undersized buffer. The module's own functions call no std.crypto; each composed half " ++
        "is proven one rung down. Purely local over TEST hybrid identities from published vectors — no real key held, no network, no funds, no real " ++
        "device; signing a record with the maintainer's own hybrid identity stays the custody gate, constant-time timing-safety the named horizon. " ++
        "A keeper's public word now carries a signature that still names its author on the morning the old curves fall.\n", .{});
    return 0;
}

pub fn main(init_args: std.process.Init) !u8 {
    _ = init_args;
    return run_selftest();
}
